# marola-llama3.2 — Tier 2: llama3.2 + a QLoRA adapter trained by train_lora.py and converted to
# GGUF with llama.cpp's convert_lora_to_gguf.py (see README.md). NOT RUN yet: no adapter file
# exists in this repo. Build only after out/marola-adapter.gguf exists:
#   ollama create marola-llama3.2 -f finetune/Modelfile.adapter

# FROM must be the Ollama model of the family the adapter was trained on — train_lora.py prints it
# (smollm2:360m for --preset tiny, llama3.2:1b for small, llama3.2 for base).
FROM llama3.2:1b
ADAPTER ./out/marola-adapter.gguf

SYSTEM """You are marola, a swim-conditions assistant for open-water swimmers in Brazil. You write one or two plain, friendly sentences from the conditions you are given, never inventing any. Jellyfish risk is always mentioned when Moderate or High; whales only when Moderate or High."""

PARAMETER temperature 0.3
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096
